    <string name="faq_background_a">Encly saves your current changes, closes the encrypted database and wipes the session key. You need to unlock again when you come back.</string>
    <string name="faq_background_q">What happens when I leave the app?</string>
    <string name="faq_biometrics_a">Use the biometrics switch in Settings → Security. Creating or removing the biometric slot requires strong biometric authentication.</string>
    <string name="faq_biometrics_q">How do I turn biometrics on or off?</string>
    <string name="faq_change_pin_a">Open Settings → Security, confirm your current PIN, then enter the new one twice.</string>
    <string name="faq_change_pin_q">How do I change my PIN?</string>
    <string name="faq_db_key_a">Encly creates a random 256-bit database key. Your PIN protects a separate AES-GCM unlock slot, and biometrics use an auth-per-use Android Keystore key.</string>
    <string name="faq_db_key_q">How is the database key protected?</string>
    <string name="faq_forgot_pin_a">If you created a recovery phrase, you can use it on the lock screen to recover access and then set a new PIN. Without a recovery slot, losing the only available key means losing the vault.</string>
    <string name="faq_forgot_pin_q">What if I forget my PIN?</string>
    <string name="faq_language_a">Open Settings → Language and pick one of the available languages, or \"System default\" to follow your device. The change applies right away.</string>
    <string name="faq_language_q">How do I change the language?</string>
    <string name="faq_new_note_a">Tap the \"+\" button on the home screen. In the editor you can use text, headings, quotes, lists, separators and links.</string>
    <string name="faq_new_note_q">How do I create a new note?</string>
    <string name="faq_recovery_phrase_a">A recovery phrase is only created in user-managed mode and is a separate way to recover the vault key. Keep it offline. Everyday unlocking uses your PIN or biometrics.</string>
    <string name="faq_recovery_phrase_q">What is the recovery phrase for?</string>
    <string name="faq_report_bug_a">Open \"About\" and use the feedback option, or write to the developer. Never include your recovery phrase, PIN or private note text in a bug report.</string>
    <string name="faq_report_bug_q">How do I report a bug?</string>
    <string name="faq_saving_a">Encly saves your changes locally and automatically. The \"Done\" button and leaving the editor also finish writing before you return to the list.</string>
    <string name="faq_saving_q">How are changes saved?</string>
    <string name="faq_screen_description">Notes, tasks, local encryption and access recovery, with no cloud sync.</string>
    <string name="faq_screen_subtitle">Answers to the most common questions</string>
    <string name="faq_screenshots_a">No. Screen protection is always on: Encly blocks screenshots, screen recording and unprotected previews in the recent apps list.</string>
    <string name="faq_screenshots_q">Can I take screenshots of Encly?</string>
    <string name="faq_section_basics">Basics</string>
    <string name="faq_section_security">Security and recovery</string>
    <string name="faq_section_settings">Settings</string>
    <string name="faq_section_troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="faq_storage_a">Notes, tags and tasks are stored only in Encly\'s local SQLCipher database. There is no cloud sync and no automatic backup: you can export an encrypted backup yourself in Settings → Backup.</string>
    <string name="faq_storage_q">Where is my data stored?</string>
    <string name="faq_tags_a">Tags help you group notes. You can create, rename, hide and delete them, and use them as a filter on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="faq_tags_q">How do tags work?</string>
    <string name="faq_tasks_a">Tasks have a description and a priority. You can filter them by priority and mark them as done. Encly never puts task text into system notifications.</string>
    <string name="faq_tasks_q">What can tasks do?</string>
    <string name="faq_theme_a">In Settings → Appearance you can choose the system, light or dark theme and, on supported Android devices, dynamic colors.</string>
    <string name="faq_theme_q">How do I change the theme?</string>
    <string name="faq_vault_damaged_a">Encly deliberately never creates an empty database over a lost or unreadable vault. Don\'t confirm the full wipe if you still need your local data.</string>
    <string name="faq_vault_damaged_q">Encly says the vault is damaged</string>

